        "1.1 AI reduces production friction; it does not remove the need for a business\nClaude can make it faster to:\n- Research a market or customer problem.\n- Turn expertise into structured material.\n- Draft documents, scripts, proposals, and training content.\n- Build and debug software with coding tools.\n- Summarise large amounts of information.\n- Design repeatable workflows.\n- Create first drafts of digital products.\n- Process repetitive writing and reading tasks.\nBut a customer still needs a reason to pay. That reason is usually one of the following:\n1. Outcome: You help them achieve a meaningful result.\n2. Time: You complete a task faster or reduce their workload.\n3. Expertise: You know how to do something they do not.\n4. Convenience: You take responsibility for a complicated process.\n5. Access: You help them reach a customer, opportunity, or capability.\n6. Trust: They believe you can deliver reliably.\nThe strongest business models in the ranking combine AI efficiency with a valuable human capability.",
